#BRUTEFORCE APPROACH

Key Idea — Brute Force Approach
Check every possible number from 0 to n.
For each number, search the entire array to see if it exists.
If the number is not found, that is the missing number.
Return that number immediately.

Time: O(n²) because of the nested loops.
Space: O(1) because you only use the flag variable.

CODE:->

class Solution {
    public int missingNumber(int[] nums) {
        for(int i = 0; i <= nums.length; i++) {
            int flag = 0;
            for(int j = 0; j < nums.length ; j++) {
                if(nums[j] == i) {
                    flag = 1;
                    break;
                }

            }
            if(flag == 0) return i;
        }
        return -1;
    }
}



#BETTER APPROACH

KEY-IDEA : Use a hash array to mark the numbers that exist, then find the index that remains unmarked.

Complexity	Value
Time       	O(n)	
Space    	O(n)

CODE:->.
class Solution {
    public int missingNumber(int[] nums) {
        int[] hash = new int[nums.length+1];

        for(int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
            hash[nums[i]] = 1;
        }
        for(int i = 0; i <= nums.length; i++) {
            if(hash[i] == 0) return i;
        }


        return -1;
    }
}


#OPTIMAL APPROACH 

##Method 1

KEY-IDEA : Expected Sum − Actual Sum = Missing Number

Complexity	Value
Time       	O(2n)	
Space    	O(1)

CODE:->

class Solution {
    public int missingNumber(int[] nums) {
        int sum = (nums.length * ( nums.length + 1)) / 2;
        int sum2 = 0;

        for(int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
            sum2 = sum2 + nums[i];
        }
        return sum - sum2;
    }
}


##Method 2

KEY-IDEA :XOR the expected numbers with the array numbers; matching numbers cancel out, leaving the missing number.

Complexity	Value
Time       	O(n)	
Space    	O(1)

CODE:->

class Solution {
    public int missingNumber(int[] nums) {
       int xor1 = 0;
       int xor2 = 0;

        for(int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
            xor2 = xor2 ^ nums[i];
            xor1 = xor1 ^ (i + 1);
        }


        return xor1 ^ xor2;
    }
}
